From 5eec3bedbbb9c32150b2be169d8f5bf85548b22b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:13:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): spend budget sends a card that keeps spending
 without a hand-off to triage [daveey]

In the 7 days to 2026-11-14 the hub default board spent 7,812 runs on 2,170
completions (3.60 runs per completion); cards with >= 10 runs that week were
24% of all fleet kanban sessions, and second-and-later sessions of one card
30% of deep-model burn. t_01a1a1dea9c64d6a ran 85 times and was still todo,
t_01a1a80b7d6cc910 73, t_7d17e13d 57. Their runs alternated continued /
blocked / scheduled / reclaimed, so neither the no-progress budget (trailing
waits only, reset by any edit, link or immediate continue; 9eb188d230) nor
the continuation cap (back-to-back `continued` only) ever stopped them:
nothing bounded the total spend of one card.

kanban_spend_budget, hooked in lane_admission_refused right after the
no-progress hold (before any claim), counts a card's spending runs (closed,
>= 60 s: quota walls, released claims and spawn failures end in seconds and
spend nothing) since it last handed work on (a run ending completed /
review_requested / changes_requested) or was last triaged by this budget, and
sums the tokens they reported. The managed worker now books its agent's
session tokens (`usage`: input/output/cache-read/cache-write, estimated cost)
on the run's worker_result receipt, on whichever host ran it, so the card's
home board sums the whole spend across workers; a run without a receipt
counts as a run only. At kanban.spend_budget_runs (default 15) or
kanban.spend_budget_cache_read_tokens (default 30M; 0 disables either), and
deciding again under the write lock, never under a live claim, the card goes
to triage with a spend_budget_triaged event and a comment showing the spend.
Triage holds it (the auto-decomposer skips cards that already ran) until
someone splits, re-scopes, archives or promotes it; a promote opens a new
window. Dispatch reports it in no_progress_held as spend_budget:triage.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_spend_budget.py 20 pass; 2 fail with the
admission hook and the worker_result usage removed (dispatch triage + the
producer receipt). Replay over the hub default board (read-only snapshot,
7 d, run-count limit only since no receipt carried usage yet): runs/completion
3.60 -> 3.28, runs 7,812 -> 7,020 (-10.1%), spending runs -9.9%; 39 cards
triaged in the week, 33 of whose later completions would need a promote.
21 open hub cards are over budget today (t_7d17e13d 217 spending runs,
t_01a19b6652a38fa7 115, t_01a1a1dea9c64d6a 113, ...) and go to triage on
their next ready tick. Card t_01a1d975f729f802.
